      "sensitivity": "non-sensitive",
      "aiSeverity": null,
      "aiValidity": null,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nThe `LaunchToken::_decreaseFeeShares()` function contains an incorrect trigger condition that prevents the rewards accrual mechanism from being properly terminated. This issue causes the `GTELaunchpadV2Pair`'s core functions (`mint()`, `burn()`, `swap()`, and `sync()`) to become permanently blocked, rendering the pair contract unusable and freezing all assets locked within it.\n\n## Finding Impact\n\n**Impact: High**\n\nThe impact is assessed as high because:\n\n1. The issue causes a permanent denial of service for critical functions of the `GTELaunchpadV2Pair` contract:\n   - `mint()` - Adding liquidity becomes impossible\n   - `burn()` - Removing liquidity becomes impossible\n   - `swap()` - Trading tokens becomes impossible\n   - `sync()` - Synchronizing reserves becomes impossible\n\n2. All launch/base tokens and quote tokens locked in the affected pairs become permanently frozen, resulting in a complete loss of funds for the token launchers (projects partnering with GTE) and other liquidity providers.\n\n3. The issue affects all pairs created for all launch tokens, making it a systemic vulnerability across the entire protocol.\n\n## Finding Likelihood\n\n**Likelihood: High**\n\nThe likelihood is assessed as high because:\n\n1. The issue is triggered by a common sequence of events in the protocol's normal operation:\n   - Launch token is created and bonded\n   - Token reaches bonding price and is graduated (unlocked = true)\n   - Users transfer their tokens, decreasing totalFeeShare to zero\n\n2. The incorrect condition is hardcoded in the core contract and will be executed for every launch token in the protocol.\n\n3. Once the launch token is graduated (unlocked = true), there is no way to call `endRewardsAccrual()` to deactivate the rewards pool, which means the issue will inevitably occur when totalFeeShare reaches zero.\n\n## Finding Description\n\nThe root cause of this issue is an incorrect trigger condition in the `LaunchToken::_decreaseFeeShares()` function:\n\n```solidity\n    // FILE: contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\n    function _decreaseFeeShares(address account, uint256 amount) internal {\n        uint256 share = bondingShare[account];\n        if (share == 0 || account == address(0)) return;\n\n        amount = amount > share ? share : amount;\n\n        emit FeeShareDecreased(account, amount, _incEventNonce());\n\n        unchecked {\n            totalFeeShare -= amount;\n            bondingShare[account] -= amount;\n        }\n\n@>      if (totalFeeShare == 0 && !unlocked) _endRewards(); //@audit -- Incorrect condition, should be (totalFeeShare == 0 && unlocked)\n\n        ILaunchpad(launchpad).decreaseStake(account, uint96(amount));\n    }\n```\n\nThe issue occurs because the condition `if (totalFeeShare == 0 && !unlocked)` is incorrect. During the bonding period (`unlocked = false`), the `totalFeeShare` tends to increase as users buy the launch token. Once the token hits the bonding price, it's graduated and the unbonding period starts (`unlocked = true`).\n\nThe correct condition should be `if (totalFeeShare == 0 && unlocked)` because:\n\n1. During the bonding period (`unlocked = false`), the pair contract doesn't exist yet, so calling `_endRewards()` would revert.\n2. The rewards program should only be ended after the token is graduated (`unlocked = true`) and no more pre-bonding shares exist (`totalFeeShare = 0`).\n\nThis incorrect condition causes the following sequence of events:\n\n1. A launch token is created and users buy tokens during the bonding period, increasing `totalFeeShare`.\n2. The token reaches its bonding price and is graduated (`unlocked = true`).\n3. After graduation, users transfer all their tokens, causing `_decreaseFeeShares()` to be called multiple times.\n4. Eventually, `totalFeeShare` reaches 0, but since `unlocked = true`, the condition `totalFeeShare == 0 && !unlocked` is never satisfied.\n5. `_endRewards()` is never called, so `GTELaunchpadV2Pair::endRewardsAccrual()` is never executed.\n6. The pair continues to accrue rewards even though there are no more shares to incentivize.\n7. When a user tries to perform a swap, mint, burn, or sync operation, the transaction reverts because:\n   - `_update()` is called\n   - `_distributeLaunchpadFees()` is called if there are accrued fees\n   - `Distributor::addRewards()` reverts with `NoSharesToIncentivize` since `rs.totalShares = 0`\n\nThe issue affects the following functions in `GTELaunchpadV2Pair`:\n\n```solidity\n    // FILE: contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\n    function mint(address to) external lock returns (uint256 liquidity) {\n        // ... code ...\n@>      _update(balance0, balance1, _reserve0, _reserve1, uint112(0), uint112(0)); //@audit -- Will revert if rs.totalShares = 0\n        // ... code ...\n    }\n\n    function burn(address to) external lock returns (uint256 amount0, uint256 amount1) {\n        // ... code ...\n@>      _update(balance0, balance1, _reserve0, _reserve1, uint112(0), uint112(0)); //@audit -- Will revert if rs.totalShares = 0\n        // ... code ...\n    }\n\n    function swap(uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out, address to, bytes calldata data) external lock {\n        // ... code ...\n@>      _update(balance0, balance1, _reserve0, _reserve1, launchpadFee0, launchpadFee1); //@audit -- Will revert if rs.totalShares = 0\n        // ... code ...\n    }\n\n    function sync() external lock {\n@>      _update(IERC20(token0).balanceOf(address(this)), IERC20(token1).balanceOf(address(this)), reserve0, reserve1, uint112(0), uint112(0)); //@audit -- Will revert if rs.totalShares = 0\n    }\n```\n\nThe revert happens in the `Distributor::addRewards()` function:\n\n```solidity\n    // FILE: contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\n    function addRewards(address token0, address token1, uint128 amount0, uint128 amount1) external {\n        // ... code ...\n\n@>      if (rs.totalShares == 0) revert NoSharesToIncentivize(); //@audit -- Reverts when no more pre-bonding shares exist\n        \n        // ... code ...\n    }\n```\n\n## Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\nFix the trigger condition in `LaunchToken::_decreaseFeeShares()`.\n\n```diff\n    function _decreaseFeeShares(address account, uint256 amount) internal {\n        uint256 share = bondingShare[account];\n        if (share == 0 || account == address(0)) return;\n\n        amount = amount > share ? share : amount;\n\n        emit FeeShareDecreased(account, amount, _incEventNonce());\n\n        unchecked {\n            totalFeeShare -= amount;\n            bondingShare[account] -= amount;\n        }\n\n-       if (totalFeeShare == 0 && !unlocked) _endRewards();\n+       if (totalFeeShare == 0 && unlocked) _endRewards();\n\n        ILaunchpad(launchpad).decreaseStake(account, uint96(amount));\n    }\n```",
      "proofOfConcept": "The PoC demonstrates the issue by:\n\n1. Creating a launch token and having a user buy enough tokens to graduate it (`unlocked = true`)\n2. Transferring all tokens to another user, which decreases `totalFeeShare` to 0\n3. Showing that the pair's `rewardsPoolActive` remains set to 1 even after `totalFeeShare = 0`\n4. Demonstrating that rewards continue to accrue\n5. Showing that subsequent calls to `swap()` and `mint()` revert with `NoSharesToIncentivize`\n\nThis confirms that the incorrect trigger condition in `_decreaseFeeShares()` causes a permanent DoS of the pair's core functions.\n\n```solidity\n// FILE: test/c4-poc/PoCLaunchpad.t.sol\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {LaunchpadTestBase} from \"./LaunchpadTestBase.sol\";\n\nimport {Distributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\";\nimport {Launchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/Launchpad.sol\";\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport {SimpleBondingCurve} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/SimpleBondingCurve.sol\";\nimport {IBondingCurveMinimal} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/IBondingCurveMinimal.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\nimport {LaunchpadLPVault} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchpadLPVault.sol\";\nimport {IDistributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IDistributor.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC1967Factory} from \"@solady/utils/ERC1967Factory.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"../harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\n\nimport {MockUniV2Router} from \"../mocks/MockUniV2Router.sol\";\n\nimport {FixedPointMathLib} from \"@solady/utils/FixedPointMathLib.sol\";\nimport {ICLOBManager} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOBManager.sol\";\nimport {IOperatorPanel} from \"contracts/utils/interfaces/IOperatorPanel.sol\";\n\nimport {UniV2Bytecode} from \"../launchpad/integration/UniV2Bytecode.t.sol\";\n\nimport \"@gte-univ2-core/interfaces/IUniswapV2Factory.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/interfaces/IGTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\n\nimport {IUniswapV2RouterMinimal} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IUniswapV2RouterMinimal.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"forge-std/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport \"@solady/utils/SafeTransferLib.sol\";\n\nimport {Test} from \"lib/forge-std/src/Test.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad is LaunchpadTestBase {\n    GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory;\n\n    // Custom setUp() for this PoC\n    function setUp() public override {\n        quoteToken = new ERC20Harness(\"Quote\", \"QTE\");\n        \n        factory = new ERC1967Factory();\n\n        bytes32 launchpadSalt = bytes32(abi.encode(\"GTE.V1.TESTNET.LAUNCHPAD\", owner));\n\n        launchpad = Launchpad(factory.predictDeterministicAddress(launchpadSalt));\n\n        address c_logic = address(new SimpleBondingCurve(address(launchpad)));\n        address v_logic = address(new LaunchpadLPVault());\n\n        curve = SimpleBondingCurve(factory.deploy(address(c_logic), owner));\n        launchpadLPVault = LaunchpadLPVault(factory.deploy(address(v_logic), owner));\n\n        address clobManager = makeAddr(\"clob manager\");\n        address operatorAddr = makeAddr(\"operator\");\n        vm.mockCall(\n            operatorAddr,\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(IOperatorPanel.getOperatorRoleApprovals.selector, user, address(0)),\n            abi.encode(0)\n        );\n\n        distributor = address(new Distributor());\n        Distributor(distributor).initialize(address(launchpad));\n\n        // Deploy the GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory instead of the mock UniV2Factory to demonstrate the vulnerability\n        gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory = new GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(address(this), address(launchpad), address(launchpadLPVault), address(distributor));\n\n        // Use the custom MockUniV2Router2 for this PoC (due to the custom addLiquidity() instead of using the C4's mock function)\n        MockUniV2Router2 uniV2Router2 = new MockUniV2Router2(address(gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory), address(launchpadLPVault), address(distributor));\n\n        address l_logic =\n            address(new Launchpad(address(uniV2Router2), address(0), clobManager, operatorAddr, distributor));\n\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        Launchpad(\n            factory.deployDeterministicAndCall({\n                implementation: l_logic,\n                admin: owner,\n                salt: launchpadSalt,\n                data: abi.encodeCall(\n                    Launchpad.initialize,\n                    (\n                        owner,\n                        address(quoteToken),\n                        address(curve),\n                        address(launchpadLPVault),\n                        abi.encode(200_000_000 ether, 10 ether)\n                    )\n                )\n            })\n        );\n\n        token = _launchToken();\n\n        BONDING_SUPPLY = curve.bondingSupply(token);\n        TOTAL_SUPPLY = curve.totalSupply(token);\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(launchpad), type(uint256).max);\n        ERC20Harness(token).approve(address(launchpad), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        launchpad.updateInitCodeHash(_getInitHash());\n    }\n\n    function _getInitHash() internal pure returns (bytes memory) {\n        bytes memory bytecode = type(GTELaunchpadV2Pair).creationCode;\n        return abi.encodePacked(keccak256(abi.encodePacked(bytecode)));\n    }\n\n    // cmd: forge test --match-test submissionValidity\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        _test_endRewardsAccrualFunc_neverBeenCalled_causesPairToBeDoSed();\n    }\n\n    function _test_endRewardsAccrualFunc_neverBeenCalled_causesPairToBeDoSed() internal {\n        // During the bonding period with totalFeeShare == 0\n        assertEq(LaunchToken(token).unlocked(), false);\n        assertEq(LaunchToken(token).totalFeeShare(), 0);\n\n        // In the bonding period, the GTELaunchpadV2Pair is not created yet\n        GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair = GTELaunchpadV2Pair(address(pairFor(address(gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory), token, address(quoteToken), address(launchpadLPVault), address(distributor))));\n        assertEq(isContract(address(pair)), false);\n\n        // User buys a huge amount of base token, making the base token graduate (during the bonding period)\n        uint256 baseAmount = BONDING_SUPPLY;\n        uint256 quoteAmount = curve.quoteQuoteForBase(token, baseAmount, true);\n        quoteToken.mint(user, quoteAmount);\n\n        vm.prank(user);\n        launchpad.buy(\n            ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n                account: user,\n                token: token,\n                recipient: user,\n                amountOutBase: baseAmount,\n                maxAmountInQuote: quoteAmount\n            })\n        );\n\n        // Now, the unbonding period starts with totalFeeShare == 800 ether\n        assertEq(LaunchToken(token).unlocked(), true);\n        assertEq(LaunchToken(token).totalFeeShare(), baseAmount);\n\n        // The GTELaunchpadV2Pair has been created with the rewardsPoolActive == 1 (activated)\n        assertEq(isContract(address(pair)), true);\n        assertEq(pair.rewardsPoolActive(), 1);\n\n        // User transfers all base tokens to another user, causing the fee shares to decrease to 0 (this is for demonstration)\n        address anotherUser = makeAddr(\"another user\");\n        vm.prank(user);\n        LaunchToken(token).transfer(anotherUser, baseAmount);\n\n        // Now, the unbonding period with the totalFeeShare decreased to 0\n        assertEq(LaunchToken(token).unlocked(), true);\n        assertEq(LaunchToken(token).totalFeeShare(), 0);\n\n        // The GTELaunchpadV2Pair remains with the rewardsPoolActive == 1 (activated)\n        assertEq(pair.rewardsPoolActive(), 1);\n\n        // Swap with the GTELaunchpadV2Pair to demonstrate the fees accrual even if the totalFeeShare is already 0 (fees accrual is expected)\n        uint256 amountIn = 10 ether;\n        quoteToken.mint(user, amountIn);\n\n        (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(quoteToken));\n\n        uint112 accruedFeeTokenBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n        uint112 accruedFeeQuoteBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n\n        pair.swap(amount0Out, amount1Out, user, hex\"\");\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1);\n        uint112 accruedFeeTokenAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n        uint112 accruedFeeQuoteAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n        assertEq(accruedFeeTokenAfter - accruedFeeTokenBefore, 0); // ==\n        assertGt(accruedFeeQuoteAfter - accruedFeeQuoteBefore, 0); // > (rewards accrued)\n\n        // Try another swap with the GTELaunchpadV2Pair (Swap revert expected)\n        amountIn = 10 ether;\n        quoteToken.mint(user, amountIn);\n\n        (amount0Out, amount1Out) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(quoteToken));\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n\n        // Expect the swap() to revert due to \"NoSharesToIncentivize\" error (the swap() is blocked indefinitely)\n        vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSelector(Distributor.NoSharesToIncentivize.selector));\n        pair.swap(amount0Out, amount1Out, user, hex\"\"); // swap() revert expected\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 10);\n\n        // Note: Furthermore, the mint(), burn(), and sync() of the GTELaunchpadV2Pair can also be permanently DoSed!\n        // The following is a demonstration of the mint() being DoSed\n        amountIn = 1 ether;\n        quoteToken.mint(user, amountIn);\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n        LaunchToken(token).transfer(address(pair), amountIn); // User has enough base token already from the first swap\n\n        // Expect the mint() to revert due to \"NoSharesToIncentivize\" error (the mint() is blocked indefinitely)\n        vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSelector(Distributor.NoSharesToIncentivize.selector));\n        pair.mint(user); // mint() revert expected\n    }\n\n    function getAmountsOut(GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair, uint256 amountIn, address tokenIn)\n        internal\n        view\n        returns (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out)\n    {\n        bool isZeroTokenIn = tokenIn == pair.token0();\n\n        (uint256 reserve0, uint256 reserve1,) = pair.getReserves();\n\n        (uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut) = isZeroTokenIn ? (reserve0, reserve1) : (reserve1, reserve0);\n        uint256 amountOut = getAmountOut(amountIn, reserveIn, reserveOut);\n        (amount0Out, amount1Out) = isZeroTokenIn ? (uint256(0), amountOut) : (amountOut, uint256(0));\n    }\n\n    function getAmountOut(uint256 amountIn, uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut)\n        internal\n        pure\n        returns (uint256 amountOut)\n    {\n        require(amountIn > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_INPUT_AMOUNT\");\n        require(reserveIn > 0 && reserveOut > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\");\n        uint256 amountInWithFee = amountIn * 997;\n        uint256 numerator = amountInWithFee * reserveOut;\n        uint256 denominator = (reserveIn * 1000) + amountInWithFee;\n        amountOut = numerator / denominator;\n    }\n\n    function pairFor(address factory, address tokenA, address tokenB, address launchpadLp, address launchpadFeeDistributor) internal view returns (IUniswapV2Pair pair) {\n        (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n        pair = IUniswapV2Pair(\n            address(\n                uint160(\n                    uint256(\n                        keccak256(\n                            abi.encodePacked(\n                                hex\"ff\",\n                                factory,\n                                keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, launchpadLp, launchpadFeeDistributor)),\n                                _getInitHash() // uniV2InitCodeHash\n                            )\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n    }\n\n    function sortTokens(address tokenA, address tokenB) internal pure returns (address token0, address token1) {\n        if (tokenA == tokenB) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: IDENTICAL_ADDRESSES\");\n        (token0, token1) = tokenA < tokenB ? (tokenA, tokenB) : (tokenB, tokenA);\n        if (token0 == address(0)) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: ZERO_ADDRESS\");\n    }\n\n    function isContract(address _addr) private returns (bool) {\n        uint32 size;\n        assembly {\n            size := extcodesize(_addr)\n        }\n        return (size > 0);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockUniV2Router2 is IUniswapV2RouterMinimal, Test {\n    using SafeTransferLib for address;\n\n    bool public constant IS_SCRIPT = true;\n    address private immutable _factory;\n    address private immutable _launchpadLPVault;\n    address private immutable _distributor;\n\n    constructor(address factory_, address launchpadLPVault_, address distributor_) {\n        _factory = factory_;\n        _launchpadLPVault = launchpadLPVault_;\n        _distributor = distributor_;\n    }\n\n    function factory() external view returns (address) {\n        return _factory;\n    }\n\n    // Custom addLiquidity() for this PoC (instead of using the C4's mock function)\n    function addLiquidity(\n        address tokenA,\n        address tokenB,\n        uint amountADesired,\n        uint amountBDesired,\n        uint amountAMin,\n        uint amountBMin,\n        address to,\n        uint deadline\n    ) external returns (uint amountA, uint amountB, uint liquidity) {\n        address pair = address(pairFor(_factory, tokenA, tokenB, _launchpadLPVault, _distributor));\n        MockERC20(tokenA).transferFrom(msg.sender, pair, amountADesired);\n        MockERC20(tokenB).transferFrom(msg.sender, pair, amountBDesired);\n\n        IUniswapV2Pair(pair).mint(to);\n\n        if (block.timestamp > deadline) revert(\"expired\");\n\n        return (0, 0, 0);\n    }\n\n    function pairFor(address factory, address tokenA, address tokenB, address launchpadLp, address launchpadFeeDistributor) internal view returns (IUniswapV2Pair pair) {\n        (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n        pair = IUniswapV2Pair(\n            address(\n                uint160(\n                    uint256(\n                        keccak256(\n                            abi.encodePacked(\n                                hex\"ff\",\n                                factory,\n                                keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, launchpadLp, launchpadFeeDistributor)),\n                                _getInitHash() // uniV2InitCodeHash\n                            )\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n    }\n\n    function sortTokens(address tokenA, address tokenB) internal pure returns (address token0, address token1) {\n        if (tokenA == tokenB) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: IDENTICAL_ADDRESSES\");\n        (token0, token1) = tokenA < tokenB ? (tokenA, tokenB) : (tokenB, tokenA);\n        if (token0 == address(0)) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: ZERO_ADDRESS\");\n    }\n\n    function _getInitHash() internal pure returns (bytes memory) {\n        bytes memory bytecode = type(GTELaunchpadV2Pair).creationCode;\n        return abi.encodePacked(keccak256(abi.encodePacked(bytecode)));\n    }\n\n    function swapExactTokensForTokens(\n        uint256 amountIn,\n        uint256, /*amountOutMin*/\n        address[] calldata path,\n        address to,\n        uint256 /*deadline*/\n    ) external returns (uint256[] memory amounts) {\n        path[0].safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amountIn);\n\n        amounts = getAmountsOut(amountIn, path);\n\n        address target = path[path.length - 1];\n\n        uint256 tokens = amounts[amounts.length - 1];\n\n        try ERC20Harness(target).mint(to, tokens) {}\n        catch {\n            vm.prank(msg.sender);\n            try LaunchToken(target).mint(tokens) {}\n            catch {\n                revert(\"cant mint mock token for swap. is not an ERC20 harness or LaunchToken\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    function swapTokensForExactTokens(uint256 amountOut, uint256, address[] calldata path, address to, uint256)\n        external\n        returns (uint256[] memory amounts)\n    {\n        uint256 amountIn = getAmountIn(amountOut, 0, 0);\n\n        path[0].safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amountIn);\n\n        address target = path[path.length - 1];\n\n        amounts = new uint256[](2);\n        amounts[0] = amountIn;\n        amounts[1] = amountOut;\n\n        try ERC20Harness(target).mint(to, amountOut) {}\n        catch {\n            vm.prank(msg.sender);\n            try LaunchToken(target).mint(amountOut) {}\n            catch {\n                revert(\"cant mint mock token for swap. is not an ERC20 harness or LaunchToken\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    function getAmountIn(uint256 amountOut, uint256, uint256) public pure returns (uint256 amountIn) {\n        amountIn = amountOut - amountIn * 1 ether / 0.5 ether;\n    }\n\n    function getAmountsOut(uint256 amountIn, address[] memory /*path*/ )\n        public\n        pure\n        returns (uint256[] memory amounts)\n    {\n        amounts = new uint256[](2);\n        amounts[0] = amountIn;\n        amounts[1] = amountIn + amountIn * 0.5 ether / 1 ether;\n    }\n}\n```",
